          %h2#introduction Introduction
          %p
            This page is to help you copy and paste special characters if you want them. For the moment, it is discouraged to put these in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/HowTo#naming"} page names
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/redirected+pages"} redirected pages
          %h2#text_symbols Text symbols
          %p Č (more to come!)
          %h2#mathematical_symbols Mathematical symbols
          %p
            These are alphabetical by the LaTeX name. If you don't know the LaTeX name, try
            %a{:href => "http://detexify.kirelabs.org/"} Detexify
            (requires Javascript). Not included are commands like
            %code \arccos
            that produce ASCII, commands like
            %code \textbullet
            that are meant for text mode (use mathmode's
            %code \bullet
            instead), and commands like
            %code \Bbbk
            that produce font and size variants.
          %p
            Although this is not intended as a list of iTeX commands (since the
            %a{:href => "http://xbeta.org/wiki/show/itex"} itex symbols list
            is pretty comprehensive and well-organised), inevitably people will use it that way too. So please place an asterisk by names that are
            %em not
            recognised by iTeX (which you will discover for yourself when you add it).
          %p Remember to use iTeX itself when appropriate. You mostly will only need to copy and paste these symbols to produce redirects (and most of the time you shouldn't have to come here since the symbol will be on the page already).
          %ul
            %li `*`: $*$
            %li `-`: $-$
            %li `|`: $|$
            %li `'`: $'$
            %li \* `&lt;`: $\lt$
            %li \* `&gt;`: $\gt$
            %li `\|`: $\|$
